# clang-tidy configuration — what the `tidy` stage of tools/ci.sh enforces.
#
# THE BUG-FINDING SUBSET, written down explicitly instead of being left to the tool's
# default. `clang-diagnostic-*` is the compiler diagnostics clang-tidy sees while it parses;
# `clang-analyzer-*` is the Clang Static Analyzer, the path-sensitive checker. Both find
# defects; neither has an opinion about style. Pinning the pair here means the check set
# cannot silently change when a new clang-tidy is installed — LLVM's built-in default is this
# same pair today (measured 2026-09-20: `clang-tidy --dump-config` with no config file in
# this repo prints `Checks: 'clang-diagnostic-*,clang-analyzer-*'`), but "today's default" is
# not a configuration.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT ENABLED — measured 2026-09-20 on this tree, 17 translation units,
# 4 cores, so that the next reader does not have to re-measure it:
#   * the stock families (-*,bugprone-*,performance-*,readability-*,modernize-*,portability-*):
#     451 findings in 387 s, 220 of them modernize-use-trailing-return-type and 136
#     modernize-use-nodiscard. Style, which .clang-format plus review already own — and a gate
#     that is red on the day it is wired gets ignored.
#   * the suite's value-only set (-*,bugprone-*,performance-*), which Computo, JSOM and
#     jsonTools run: 53 findings in 204 s here. 9 are the known
#     bugprone-unchecked-optional-access false positives on GoogleTest
#     `ASSERT_TRUE(opt.has_value())` guards, 11 are ONE decision about the published API
#     (performance-enum-size wants a narrower base type for MissingKeyBehavior, reported once
#     per TU that includes the header), and the rest are minor. Adopting it here is an OPEN
#     decision, not a forgotten one; until it is made, this repo's tidy certifies the
#     analyzer's defects and nothing else. Numbers and the decision record:
#     INCIDENTS.md, .ci.env.example.
#
# There is no baseline file, on purpose: with the check set below this tree is clean, and a
# baseline tolerates findings you inherited — it does not bless a rule set. If a finding ever
# does have to be accepted, accept it through the gate (`tools/ci.sh --write-tidy-baseline`),
# never by hand.
Checks: 'clang-diagnostic-*,clang-analyzer-*'

# Which INCLUDED files get reported. A positive pattern for this repo's own tree, the same
# shape Computo/JSOM/jsonTools use, and for the same reason: the paths in the compilation
# database are absolute and matched as substrings, so `Permuto/(src|include|tests|examples|cli)/`
# cannot appear inside a dependency's path while it does appear in any checkout of this repo
# (the directory is named Permuto in every clone). Diagnostics raised in the analysed .cpp
# itself are reported regardless of this filter, so relocating a clone cannot lose this repo's
# own source findings — only header findings depend on the directory still being named Permuto.
HeaderFilterRegex: 'Permuto/(src|include|tests|examples|cli)/.*\.(hpp|cpp)$'
